  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1158 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nAnother beautiful, dry day is on display across the Mid-South\nwith temperatures currently spanning the 60s. RH values will\ncontinue to dip into the afternoon hours, with high temperatures\nexpected to rise back into the 70s for many today. With the\ngenerally low RH values and little to no precipitation recently,\nelevated fire danger concerns will arise once again this\nafternoon and through much of the upcoming week. As such, be sure\nto obey all local burn bans and outdoor burning / activities that\ninvolve open sparks or flames are discouraged.\n\nAs far as the rest of the forecast, very little changes are\nexpected. A low pressure system will remain off the East Coast\nthrough much of the week, with a building upper-level ridge to\nour west. This overall pattern will aid to keep the Mid-South dry\nfor the foreseeable future, with temperatures gradually warming\nthrough midweek before camping in the upper 70s to low 80s into\nthe upcoming weekend. This pattern will likely persist into the\nupcoming week as the upper-level ridge drifts eastward across the\nregion. There is some small variability in LREF guidance that\ncould mean the difference of a few degrees with our high\ntemperatures over the weekend. However, high temperatures will\nremain above-normal regardless. For those curious about the end\nof the month, the latest 8 to 14 day outlook from CPC does have\nthe Mid-South with above-normal temperatures favored. So, it\nappears any true cold weather will continue to hold off through\nat least the end of October.",
